{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"doctoral-wandering-velvetworm","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe \"create-exclusive lock file, write a v2 owner stamp, reclaim once if stale\" loop exists twice, structurally identical (~45 LOC each): `src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py:129-176` (`_acquire_advisory_lock`) and `src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py:150-204` (`_acquire_trigger_lock`), both calling `rebar._store.lock_owner.stamped_file_is_stale`. The copy was how the unresolved-path defect spread (bug `nuclear-calm-heron`), and `knavish-stimulated-bluebottle` recorded the loop as a third locking dialect beside `_store/lock.py`.\n\n## Approach\nExtract `src/rebar/_store/stamped_lock.py` with `stamped_file_lock(path, *, label=None) -> int | None` and `release(fd, path)`, owning the O_EXCL create, stamp write, single stale-reclaim, and the documented accepted race; `enrich_drain` and `compact_trigger` become three-line callers. Sits beside `lock_owner.py`, which stays the staleness authority. Guard test: `os.O_EXCL` combined with `stamped_file_is_stale` appears only in `stamped_lock.py` (owner excluded; `# stamped-lock-ok:` marker escape).\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_store/stamped_lock.py` (new), `src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py`, `tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: acquire, second acquire refused, release, acquire again. Edge: stale stamp (dead pid) is reclaimed exactly once; a live stamp is never reclaimed. Pinning: `tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py::test_drain_and_doctor_describe_a_holderless_lock_identically`, `tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py`, `tests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py`, `tests/unit/test_lock_age_ceiling.py` pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `grep -rn \"O_EXCL\" src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py` is empty; checked by the grep and the guard test.\n- [ ] The drain and the compaction worker still refuse each other's concurrent run and still reclaim a dead holder; checked by the existing pinning tests.\n- [ ] Net non-test LOC change is negative; checked by `git show --numstat`.\n","id":"1cf6-f902-5bfa-438f","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","priority":2,"tags":["consolidation","janitor","fortnight-review"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"One stamped-file lock shared by the enrichment drain and the compaction worker"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787352100067274001,"uuid":"f7bd0812-8a0b-4f13-8357-758346d6f1ff"}